A few thoughts:

Overflowing fountains should make this instead of deep water. (Unless 
there was already a pit.)
Digging in or next to shallow water makes deep water.
Zapping fire at shallow water makes floor.
Pushing a boulder in deep water, might leave shallow water behind, or 
even flood other floor tiles with it.
Destroying a water elemental could leave shallow water on that square.
Marshy rooms should contain some combination of deep, shallow and dry 
squares.

Questions:

Can you be drowned in it? (By a Couatl, for example.)
If you dig next to it, as above, should the shallow water go away?

